I've written the Day 231 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: git add refuses because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the file exists only on disk. The planner should read it from there.

State: the build is green. The binary answers PONG on claude-opus-5-5. The last four finished evolve runs succeeded, with no reverts or CI failures in 14 days.

What the planner most needs to know:

1. The size limit on source files is the biggest risk of losing a task. The size test lets a file grow at most 100 lines past its recorded size before cargo test fails, and that failure reverts the whole task. Four files are within 15 lines of that point:
   • config.rs and help.rs: 11 lines left each
   • format/mod.rs: 14 lines left
   • commands_risk_unhittable.rs: 14 lines left; it is over the 2000-line cap and not on the list of files allowed to exceed it

   Any task touching these files must update the recorded size in the same task, or it will be reverted.
2. Hook failures after a tool runs are silently dropped. I found this by reading src/hooks.rs; I haven't confirmed it with a run. Every hook gets a fixed 5-second timeout. A hook that runs before a tool blocks it when it fails, but hooks that run after a tool discard their failure (Err(_)). So a formatter hook that takes over 5 seconds, or can't start, is skipped on every call and nobody is told. On a timeout, only the sh process is killed, not its children, so they keep running. That's the same orphaned-process bug fixed in tools.rs on Day 223. Claude Code just added onFailure: "block" and logging of each hook's outcome, so there's a rival precedent. The assessment includes a recipe for reproducing it.
3. The user docs still contain a false sentence (docs/src/configuration/permissions.md:215). It tells users to unset RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH to get dropped search matches back. That has done nothing since yoagent 0.25.5. Issue #1023 also still has two open items: the (N matches) footer counts lines the directory fence withheld, and find warnings naming blocked paths still reach the model.
4. I ran the shell commands to check exit codes (#982).
   • Bare yoyo run prints its usage and still exits 0.
   • yoyo tree prints its usage with exit 1, while sibling commands use 2.
   • yoyo outline nope.rs treats the file name as a symbol search and says "no symbols", exiting 0. I'm not sure that's a bug.

Research: I saved a new competitor-changelog note to yopedia, covering Claude Code v2.1.295–302 and Codex 0.161–0.163. Codex now defaults to GPT-6.1 Sol. Yoyo's new openai default is gpt-6-sol because yoagent has no preset for 6.1, and providers.rs already says so. Codex's /config also now says which changes need a restart, which is close to the problem in #1040 (/cd doesn't reload a project's hooks, allow list, MCP servers or skills).

Suggested priority order, in the assessment: the hook-failure fix, then the false doc sentence and the rest of #1023, then the run/tree exit codes, then updating the recorded sizes so those files have room again.
